in AD","nucleus_padj":0.0291874,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.138951,"nucleus_score":-2.40769,"pct_ad":0.0986388,"pct_control":0.10839,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.990423,"donor_log2fc":-0.0404978,"donor_lfcse":0.11282,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-1.5061e-06}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000140950","entrez_id":["57707"],"uniprot":["Q6P9B6"],"ncbi_summary":"Involved in several processes, including TOR signaling; positive regulation of protein localization to lysosome; and response to insulin. Located in cytosol; lysosomal membrane; and nuclear lumen. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6P9B6","text":"Activates an alternative mTOR signaling pathway through RPS6KB2 activation and EIF4EBP1 repression to regulate cell proliferation and migration (PubMed:29750193). Recruits MTOR at the lysosome, essential for MTOR signaling at the lysosome (PubMed:29750193). Binds to the vacuolar-type ATPase (V-ATPase) complex, triggering a conformational change and is likely to regulate its activity (PubMed:35672408, PubMed:35994636). No effect on V-ATPase activity was observed in vitro in one study although it was suggested that it may have inhibitory activity in vivo (PubMed:35672408). However, another study showed that it can promote V-ATPase activity (PubMed:38593795). Protects neuronal cells against oxidative stress (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}